From: FireTabs contributors
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mt8163: correct memory and cooling declarations

Give the memory node the unit address matching its existing reg base and
supply the two cooling cells used by the CPU cooling-map references.
Preserve the donor memory size and voltages; runtime memory, CPU policy
registration and thermal safety still require separate board validation.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8163-amazon-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8163-amazon-common.dtsi
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
 		default-brightness-level = <512>;
 	};
 
-	memory {
+	memory@40000000 {
 		device_type = "memory";
 		reg = <0 0x40000000 0 0x20000000>;
 	};
@@ -62,18 +62,22 @@
 };
 
 &cpu0 {
+	#cooling-cells = <2>;
 	proc-supply = <&sym827_vproc>;
 };
 
 &cpu1 {
+	#cooling-cells = <2>;
 	proc-supply = <&sym827_vproc>;
 };
 
 &cpu2 {
+	#cooling-cells = <2>;
 	proc-supply = <&sym827_vproc>;
 };
 
 &cpu3 {
+	#cooling-cells = <2>;
 	proc-supply = <&sym827_vproc>;
 };
 
